      "id": 1,
      "text": "White's City was founded by businessman Charlie White in the early 1900s, right next to the entrance of Carlsbad Caverns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://whitescitynm.com/whites-city/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original White’s City Cavern Camp started with a single home, 13 visitor units, and a fueling station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://whitescitynm.com/whites-city/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Whites City is the last fuel station between Carlsbad and El Paso, making it a vital pit stop for long‑haul drivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://whitescitynm.com/whites-city/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early attractions in White’s City included a chair lift up Walnut Canyon, a melodrama theatre, the Million Dollar Museum, and the Velvet Garter Saloon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://whitescitynm.com/whites-city/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Over the decades, White’s City has undergone dramatic renovations to restore its historic richness and cultural uniqueness.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://whitescitynm.com/whites-city/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
